1
00:00:04,613 --> 00:00:05,657
The red light's on.

2
00:00:05,744 --> 00:00:07,485
T-that means
we're ready, yeah?

3
00:00:07,572 --> 00:00:09,052
'Yes.'

4
00:00:09,139 --> 00:00:11,185
Would you,
uh, tell us why and how

5
00:00:11,272 --> 00:00:13,317
a psychic
becomes a CBI agent?

6
00:00:13,404 --> 00:00:15,232
I'm not a psychic.

7
00:00:15,319 --> 00:00:16,755
No such things as psychics.

8
00:00:16,842 --> 00:00:18,366
And he's not a CBI agent.

9
00:00:18,453 --> 00:00:19,715
He's a consultant.

10
00:00:19,802 --> 00:00:21,456
Big difference.

11
00:00:21,543 --> 00:00:22,587
"No such thing as psychics."

12
00:00:22,674 --> 00:00:26,461
Uh, care to elaborate?

13
00:00:30,726 --> 00:00:32,684
Uh, no, not particularly.

14
00:00:32,771 --> 00:00:36,036
Um...you know what,
this-this is not..

15
00:00:36,123 --> 00:00:37,602
This is not a good idea,
I don't think..

16
00:00:37,689 --> 00:00:40,431
Um, not a good idea.

17
00:00:40,518 --> 00:00:41,737
[clears throat]
'Okay.'

18
00:00:41,824 --> 00:00:43,173
'Um, maybe we'll-we'll'

19
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:44,566
'come back to that later.'

20
00:00:44,653 --> 00:00:47,699
'Uh, how do your
cases usually start?'

21
00:00:47,786 --> 00:00:50,050
Uh, a case begins with
us getting a phone call

22
00:00:50,137 --> 00:00:51,312
from the AG's office

23
00:00:51,399 --> 00:00:52,791
to lead an investigation.

24
00:00:52,878 --> 00:00:54,054
In the St. Clare homicide

25
00:00:54,141 --> 00:00:55,577
the local DA wanted us on it

26
00:00:55,664 --> 00:00:57,883
because there were
political issues involved.

27
00:00:57,970 --> 00:00:59,929
And how did
the local cops feel

28
00:01:00,016 --> 00:01:02,584
about your-your team
coming in?

29
00:01:02,671 --> 00:01:04,368
We get along extremely well

30
00:01:04,455 --> 00:01:07,676
with our local partners
in law enforcement, yes.

31
00:01:07,763 --> 00:01:10,418
My people can handle this,
no problem.

32
00:01:10,505 --> 00:01:12,333
California Bureau of
Interference is what you are.

33
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:13,682
Interference?

34
00:01:13,769 --> 00:01:15,118
- That's witty.
- Stay out of this.

35
00:01:15,205 --> 00:01:17,338
I'm sure your people are
competent, Chief Donner.

36
00:01:17,425 --> 00:01:19,296
We're simply following
the AG's orders.

37
00:01:19,383 --> 00:01:20,863
Screw the AG.

38
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:22,386
This case is going
to be in the news

39
00:01:22,473 --> 00:01:23,692
and you people are
spotlight hogs.

40
00:01:23,779 --> 00:01:25,433
- That's all.
- I assure you, chief--

41
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:26,912
Don't waste your time,
his anger runs

42
00:01:26,999 --> 00:01:29,045
deeper than you can reach.

43
00:01:29,132 --> 00:01:30,742
Seriously,
don't start trouble here.

44
00:01:30,829 --> 00:01:32,135
It's the last
thing we need.

45
00:01:32,222 --> 00:01:34,485
The victim is
Martha St. Clare, 34.

46
00:01:34,572 --> 00:01:35,530
Media relations coordinator

47
00:01:35,617 --> 00:01:36,879
'for the mayor of this town.'

48
00:01:36,966 --> 00:01:37,880
Mayor was here
to break ground

49
00:01:37,967 --> 00:01:39,055
on a new development.

50
00:01:39,142 --> 00:01:40,361
Dug up her PR flack instead.

51
00:01:40,448 --> 00:01:41,710
Ouch.

52
00:01:41,797 --> 00:01:42,928
Yeah, victim was stabbed
twice in the chest

53
00:01:43,015 --> 00:01:44,060
but there's
no blood here.

54
00:01:44,147 --> 00:01:45,148
Killed elsewhere.

55
00:01:45,235 --> 00:01:46,671
Home.

56
00:01:46,758 --> 00:01:48,325
Her nails are done.
Her hair's done.

57
00:01:48,412 --> 00:01:50,197
This woman doesn't
wear sweatpants anywhere

58
00:01:50,284 --> 00:01:51,589
but at home.

59
00:01:51,676 --> 00:01:53,287
Cho, have Van Pelt
check it out.

60
00:01:53,374 --> 00:01:54,288
Yeah.

61
00:01:56,638 --> 00:01:58,727
The killer wanted
the body to be discovered here

62
00:01:58,814 --> 00:02:00,381
under the glare
of the cameras.

63
00:02:00,468 --> 00:02:02,644
And likely came here
to watch the fuss.

64
00:02:02,731 --> 00:02:04,167
Likely.

65
00:02:04,254 --> 00:02:06,126
Maybe the camera crews
caught something.

66
00:02:06,213 --> 00:02:07,953
We'll need to have
them look into it.

67
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:09,259
[sniffing]

68
00:02:09,346 --> 00:02:10,869
There's bruises on her arms.

69
00:02:10,956 --> 00:02:12,480
Looks like something
was ripped off her neck

70
00:02:12,567 --> 00:02:14,090
during the struggle.

71
00:02:14,177 --> 00:02:15,831
Is he sniffing her?

72
00:02:15,918 --> 00:02:17,267
Yes.

73
00:02:17,354 --> 00:02:19,182
You pay him to sniff people?

74
00:02:19,269 --> 00:02:20,314
Apparently.

75
00:02:20,401 --> 00:02:23,055
She's been smoking.

76
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,448
The nicotine
patch on her arm

77
00:02:24,535 --> 00:02:25,580
says she
was trying to quit.

78
00:02:25,667 --> 00:02:27,059
So under
stress of late.

79
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:29,236
Well, case closed.

80
00:02:29,323 --> 00:02:31,107
Stress got a knife
and stabbed her to death.

81
00:02:31,194 --> 00:02:32,978
He's on a roll.

82
00:02:33,065 --> 00:02:34,023
You're on a roll.

83
00:02:34,110 --> 00:02:35,416
[sniffs]
Cheap soap.

84
00:02:35,503 --> 00:02:36,895
Unironed shirt.
Stomach pains.

85
00:02:36,982 --> 00:02:38,070
Recent loss of weight.

86
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,855
I'm gonna
take a wild guess here.

87
00:02:39,942 --> 00:02:41,073
You're angry
and unhappy

88
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,379
'cause you're
living in a motel

89
00:02:42,466 --> 00:02:43,728
because your wife
found out about the woman

90
00:02:43,815 --> 00:02:44,773
you're having
an affair with

91
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,122
that you don't
even care for.

92
00:02:46,209 --> 00:02:47,950
You're a seething mass
of self-loathing

93
00:02:48,037 --> 00:02:49,212
and understandably so.

94
00:02:50,822 --> 00:02:52,346
You son of a bitch!

95
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:53,825
Donner,
my apologies.

96
00:02:53,912 --> 00:02:55,740
He was completely
out of line.

97
00:02:55,827 --> 00:02:59,440
Let-let's just get
back to the body. Sir?

98
00:03:00,397 --> 00:03:03,139
[theme music]

99
00:03:13,105 --> 00:03:14,063
We've closed more cases

100
00:03:14,150 --> 00:03:15,934
than any other unit in the CBI.

101
00:03:16,021 --> 00:03:17,893
But we don't
keep score that way.

102
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:20,025
It's not a contest.

103
00:03:20,112 --> 00:03:22,767
And you-you also...lead

104
00:03:22,854 --> 00:03:24,116
in the number of complaints

105
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:26,641
'and lawsuits filed.'

106
00:03:27,729 --> 00:03:30,601
Okay, hold it.

107
00:03:30,688 --> 00:03:34,039
I thought we had an agreement.

108
00:03:34,126 --> 00:03:35,563
Brenda, a word.

109
00:03:41,786 --> 00:03:43,832
Jane's right.
This isn't a good idea.

110
00:03:43,919 --> 00:03:45,616
I thought this was supposed
to be positive coverage.

111
00:03:45,703 --> 00:03:47,096
It is! It will be.

112
00:03:47,183 --> 00:03:48,880
If we're open
and honest about the issues

113
00:03:48,967 --> 00:03:51,318
the positivity follows.
That's PR 101.

114
00:03:51,405 --> 00:03:52,449
We're trying to solve

115
00:03:52,536 --> 00:03:54,103
a woman's murder here, Brenda.

116
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:56,279
We don't have time
to waste on PR.

117
00:03:56,366 --> 00:03:58,194
Teresa, you know that we have

118
00:03:58,281 --> 00:03:59,500
been crucified by the media

119
00:03:59,587 --> 00:04:01,197
ever since Bosco
and his team were killed

120
00:04:01,284 --> 00:04:02,938
'here in our own house.'

121
00:04:03,025 --> 00:04:04,113
'When KTQZ asked me'

122
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,201
for access yesterday

123
00:04:05,288 --> 00:04:07,116
I jumped at it.

124
00:04:07,203 --> 00:04:10,075
And the deputy AG concurred.

125
00:04:10,162 --> 00:04:11,642
Who is this guy anyway?

126
00:04:11,729 --> 00:04:14,210
Totally legit,
TV investigative reporter

127
00:04:14,297 --> 00:04:15,864
'Mike Brewster.'

128
00:04:15,951 --> 00:04:19,302
He has been covering
the central valley for years.

129
00:04:19,389 --> 00:04:20,521
We need this.

130
00:04:20,608 --> 00:04:22,523
Teresa. Please.
Work with us.

131
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:24,220
He stays out of my way.

132
00:04:24,307 --> 00:04:26,091
He can film in the office
and in the bullpen

133
00:04:26,178 --> 00:04:27,484
but not out in the field.

134
00:04:27,571 --> 00:04:29,007
Thank you.

135
00:04:29,094 --> 00:04:31,096
Seriously, thank you.

136
00:04:31,183 --> 00:04:33,185
You won't be sorry,
and it's a two-way street.

137
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:36,101
Agent Lisbon, if there's
anything I can do for you.

138
00:04:36,188 --> 00:04:38,408
There is one thing.

139
00:04:38,495 --> 00:04:39,757
[Brewster]
Okay, so this is
the footage Steve and I

140
00:04:39,844 --> 00:04:40,932
grabbed of the groundbreaking.

141
00:04:41,019 --> 00:04:42,369
That's the mayor.

142
00:04:42,456 --> 00:04:44,284
'Melba, Walker, Shannon.'

143
00:04:44,371 --> 00:04:45,894
She plays up the folksy image

144
00:04:45,981 --> 00:04:47,635
but she'd be tough as nails,
if she needs to be.

145
00:04:47,722 --> 00:04:50,246
Nice shoes.
Chip?

146
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,117
No, thanks. Who's the rich guy
next to the mayor?

147
00:04:52,204 --> 00:04:53,597
'Oh, that's Heaton Krupp.'

148
00:04:53,684 --> 00:04:54,990
He's the private
developer on the project.

149
00:04:55,077 --> 00:04:57,166
Off the record, a prize jerk.

150
00:04:57,253 --> 00:04:59,647
- Who are those people?
- 'Tree huggers.'

151
00:04:59,734 --> 00:05:01,736
'The project's going up on the
edge of some reclaimed land.'

152
00:05:01,823 --> 00:05:03,520
You mean protected wildlands.

153
00:05:03,607 --> 00:05:05,479
You say "potato."

154
00:05:05,566 --> 00:05:07,307
You have any other
footage of the crowds?

155
00:05:07,394 --> 00:05:08,786
Not really.
Other networks might.

156
00:05:08,873 --> 00:05:10,135
But gaining access
can be tricky.

157
00:05:10,222 --> 00:05:11,963
It'd be good to get
a different perspective.

158
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:13,443
Cho, see if you can
get the footage.

159
00:05:13,530 --> 00:05:15,010
You got it.

160
00:05:15,097 --> 00:05:16,533
'Alright,
that's Wilson Fonteneau.'

161
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:17,839
The mayor's flunky.

162
00:05:17,926 --> 00:05:21,321
And here comes the money shot.

163
00:05:31,635 --> 00:05:32,549
Oh.

164
00:05:36,727 --> 00:05:38,425
[button clicks]

165
00:05:38,512 --> 00:05:40,035
These are from
the victim's home.

166
00:05:40,122 --> 00:05:41,471
Besides the signs
of a scuffle

167
00:05:41,558 --> 00:05:42,603
the only thing that
seemed to be missing

168
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:44,082
was the victim's laptop.

169
00:05:44,169 --> 00:05:45,693
The murderer
probably took it.

170
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:47,085
Check out this necklace.

171
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:52,352
From the photos, it looks
like she wore it a lot.

172
00:05:52,439 --> 00:05:54,005
You think it could have
made the mark on her neck?

173
00:05:54,092 --> 00:05:55,659
Could be, when you
go to the apartment

174
00:05:55,746 --> 00:05:57,052
do a targeted search.

175
00:05:57,139 --> 00:05:58,706
The necklace is long gone.

176
00:05:58,793 --> 00:06:00,925
My guess, killer
made a souvenir of it.

177
00:06:01,012 --> 00:06:03,058
- Go.
- Okay.

178
00:06:03,145 --> 00:06:04,407
Where we going?

179
00:06:04,494 --> 00:06:05,756
Mayor's office.

180
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,805
I don't have any problem
being in charge, no.

181
00:06:10,892 --> 00:06:14,199
I mean, maybe,
at first for a while

182
00:06:14,286 --> 00:06:15,766
as a woman,
it was a challenge.

183
00:06:15,853 --> 00:06:19,727
But...the demands
of the job take over. Yeah.

184
00:06:19,814 --> 00:06:22,077
[Brewster]
'Tell me about your weekends.'

185
00:06:22,164 --> 00:06:24,253
You wanna know
what I do on my weekends?

186
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:26,081
'Yeah.'

187
00:06:26,168 --> 00:06:28,910
Why do you want to know that?

188
00:06:28,997 --> 00:06:30,781
I mean, I have
no problem having a life.

189
00:06:30,868 --> 00:06:32,130
If that's what you mean.

190
00:06:32,217 --> 00:06:33,305
I don't know why anybody

191
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:34,350
would say otherwise.

192
00:06:34,437 --> 00:06:36,526
If they do...say otherwise.

193
00:06:36,613 --> 00:06:38,876
Um, I'm...I'm sorry.

194
00:06:38,963 --> 00:06:40,704
What were we talking about?

195
00:06:40,791 --> 00:06:43,185
[theme music]

196
00:06:49,583 --> 00:06:51,062
Sorry for the delay.

197
00:06:51,149 --> 00:06:52,455
The mayor's just
finishing up another meeting.

198
00:06:52,542 --> 00:06:54,196
It's been
a crazy day around here.

199
00:06:54,283 --> 00:06:55,415
Can I help you?

200
00:06:55,502 --> 00:06:57,242
Oh, no, I'm fine. Thanks.

201
00:06:57,329 --> 00:06:59,506
[Lisbon]
'Mr. Fonteneau,
did you work closely'

202
00:06:59,593 --> 00:07:00,942
'with Martha St. Clare?'

203
00:07:01,029 --> 00:07:03,118
For 16 months.

204
00:07:03,205 --> 00:07:04,598
Martha hired me,
actually.

205
00:07:04,685 --> 00:07:06,991
We noticed in a lot
of recent photographs

206
00:07:07,078 --> 00:07:08,732
that she had
a-a necklace on

207
00:07:08,819 --> 00:07:10,168
with a beautiful stone.

208
00:07:10,255 --> 00:07:12,301
Yes, a topaz, I think.

209
00:07:12,388 --> 00:07:13,563
It was her birthstone.

210
00:07:13,650 --> 00:07:15,130
She got it
Christmas of last year

211
00:07:15,217 --> 00:07:16,218
and never took it off.

212
00:07:16,305 --> 00:07:17,611
Do you know
who gave it to her?

213
00:07:17,698 --> 00:07:19,090
- No.
- She had a lot of meetings.

214
00:07:19,177 --> 00:07:20,570
Even on weekends.

215
00:07:20,657 --> 00:07:23,312
Business interests,
community groups, book club.

216
00:07:23,399 --> 00:07:24,922
Tomorrow is a big day.

217
00:07:25,009 --> 00:07:27,795
She has a star and three
exclamation marks at eleven.

218
00:07:27,882 --> 00:07:29,013
Yes.

219
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,233
Uh, she scheduled
a briefing

220
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,495
with the city council.

221
00:07:32,582 --> 00:07:33,757
On what subject?

222
00:07:33,844 --> 00:07:35,237
I don't know,
to be honest.

223
00:07:35,324 --> 00:07:36,934
The mayor will know.

224
00:07:37,021 --> 00:07:38,806
Was she dating anyone?

225
00:07:38,893 --> 00:07:41,243
A social life? Martha?

226
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:42,940
No, she had a cat.

227
00:07:43,027 --> 00:07:44,855
Ah. Yes.

228
00:07:44,942 --> 00:07:46,770
But it died.

229
00:07:46,857 --> 00:07:48,076
Right.

230
00:07:48,163 --> 00:07:49,991
Excuse me.
Are you the CBI agents?

231
00:07:50,078 --> 00:07:51,427
Mayor, thank you
for seeing us.

232
00:07:51,514 --> 00:07:53,429
Happy to help,
and please call me Melba.

233
00:07:53,516 --> 00:07:55,387
Like the toast?

234
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:57,302
Just like.
This way.

235
00:08:03,265 --> 00:08:05,223
Can you tell us about
your construction project

236
00:08:05,310 --> 00:08:06,703
that you were
opening yesterday?

237
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:08,836
It's the Granton Complex.

238
00:08:08,923 --> 00:08:10,707
Yes, we areveryproud of it.

239
00:08:10,794 --> 00:08:12,840
'It's office and retail space'

240
00:08:12,927 --> 00:08:14,624
'plus housing, all built'

241
00:08:14,711 --> 00:08:16,974
with the latest
green technology.

242
00:08:17,061 --> 00:08:19,281
And what was Martha's
involvement in the project?

243
00:08:19,368 --> 00:08:22,719
None, really, she..

244
00:08:22,806 --> 00:08:24,199
...she was my..

245
00:08:24,286 --> 00:08:25,243
...media liaison.

246
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:26,680
She was not engaged

247
00:08:26,767 --> 00:08:28,943
in policy issues.

248
00:08:29,030 --> 00:08:30,161
Then what
was she gonna talk

249
00:08:30,248 --> 00:08:32,729
about at city council tomorrow?

250
00:08:32,816 --> 00:08:34,470
Oh, a press junket.

251
00:08:34,557 --> 00:08:36,951
It was river rafting,
I believe.

252
00:08:37,038 --> 00:08:38,387
'Chief Donner says your office'

253
00:08:38,474 --> 00:08:39,780
has received several threats

254
00:08:39,867 --> 00:08:41,042
from environmental activists.

255
00:08:41,129 --> 00:08:42,217
Activists?

256
00:08:42,304 --> 00:08:44,001
No, they're terrorists.

257
00:08:44,088 --> 00:08:46,787
They burned down vacation
condos up on the mountain.

258
00:08:46,874 --> 00:08:49,703
'They destroyed luxury car
lots just one town over.'

259
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:52,923
They're led by a madman,
and he calls himself Jasper.

260
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:54,577
- Uh..
- Excuse me.

261
00:08:57,319 --> 00:08:59,713
Wilson, anything else can wait.

262
00:09:05,501 --> 00:09:06,676
- The threats?
- 'Yes.'

263
00:09:06,763 --> 00:09:07,895
'Um..'

264
00:09:12,029 --> 00:09:16,207
The Granton development
is an abomination.

265
00:09:16,294 --> 00:09:20,211
'A hundred acres
of pristine wildlands razed.'

266
00:09:20,298 --> 00:09:22,344
'An entire
ecosystem endangered.'

267
00:09:22,431 --> 00:09:24,259
It must stop.

268
00:09:24,346 --> 00:09:28,219
It will stop, no matter
what needs to be done.

269
00:09:28,306 --> 00:09:30,918
My name is Jasper..

270
00:09:31,005 --> 00:09:34,138
...and I am legion.

271
00:09:34,225 --> 00:09:35,923
[chuckling]
Come on.

272
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:38,012
"I am legion."
That's just silly.

273
00:09:38,099 --> 00:09:39,970
- Silly?
- Yeah.

274
00:09:40,057 --> 00:09:41,015
He murdered Martha.

275
00:09:41,102 --> 00:09:42,103
Well, you assume.

276
00:09:42,190 --> 00:09:43,583
Yes, I do.

277
00:09:43,670 --> 00:09:45,759
The body was buried
at the site, for God's sake.

278
00:09:45,846 --> 00:09:47,108
And that is
a clear message.

279
00:09:47,195 --> 00:09:48,413
Isn't it?

280
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,198
Melba..

281
00:09:50,285 --> 00:09:52,287
...why would
he kill Martha..

282
00:09:52,374 --> 00:09:53,462
...and not kill you?

283
00:09:53,549 --> 00:09:56,247
It'd be a bigger
publicity coup.

284
00:09:56,334 --> 00:09:57,335
Excuse me?

285
00:09:57,422 --> 00:09:59,511
What Mr. Jane
is trying to ask

286
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,296
is whether there was
somebody with a more

287
00:10:01,383 --> 00:10:03,124
direct personal
grudge against Martha.

288
00:10:03,211 --> 00:10:04,821
- Mm.
- Yeah.

289
00:10:04,908 --> 00:10:06,170
No.

290
00:10:06,257 --> 00:10:08,042
She was a lovely..

291
00:10:08,129 --> 00:10:09,565
...was a lovely person.

292
00:10:09,652 --> 00:10:11,480
Oh, then why did you
dislike her so much?

293
00:10:11,567 --> 00:10:14,657
I didn't dislike Martha.

294
00:10:14,744 --> 00:10:16,920
Why would I employ
someone that...I don't like?

295
00:10:17,007 --> 00:10:18,400
Well, that's
a very good question.

296
00:10:18,487 --> 00:10:19,836
When you said it,
your jaw tensed

297
00:10:19,923 --> 00:10:21,185
and your eyes went
empty like a cobra.

298
00:10:21,272 --> 00:10:22,970
Wilson!

299
00:10:23,057 --> 00:10:24,275
I'm not saying you killed her,
I'm just saying

300
00:10:24,362 --> 00:10:25,625
that you're relieved
that she's dead.

301
00:10:25,712 --> 00:10:27,409
These people
will be leaving now.

302
00:10:27,496 --> 00:10:28,802
I like the way
you say that.

303
00:10:28,889 --> 00:10:30,630
Melba like the toast,
so tough and commanding.

304
00:10:30,717 --> 00:10:31,848
Now, let me tell you something.

305
00:10:31,935 --> 00:10:33,633
We are state
law enforcement

306
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,025
and we leave
when we want to leave.

307
00:10:35,112 --> 00:10:36,331
Thank you for your time.

308
00:10:36,418 --> 00:10:38,289
She wants to leave.

309
00:10:40,074 --> 00:10:41,379
See you.

310
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:46,994
You blew my cool.

311
00:10:47,081 --> 00:10:49,213
I swear, sometimes
I think you need medication.

312
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:50,867
It's like you've got
ADD or something.

313
00:10:50,954 --> 00:10:52,086
Well, "A,"
I'm not so sure that

314
00:10:52,173 --> 00:10:53,609
ADD even exists

315
00:10:53,696 --> 00:10:55,611
and "B," I was winding
her up for a reason.

316
00:10:55,698 --> 00:10:57,482
- Which is?
- A diversion.

317
00:10:57,569 --> 00:10:59,136
The message the aide
brought in made her nervous.

318
00:10:59,223 --> 00:11:00,790
- So I took it.
- You're stealing now?

319
00:11:00,877 --> 00:11:02,531
Well, let's just
call it purloining.

320
00:11:02,618 --> 00:11:03,619
What does it say?

321
00:11:03,706 --> 00:11:05,839
It says,
"Your 3 o'clock meeting

322
00:11:05,926 --> 00:11:07,449
has now
been moved to 3:15."

323
00:11:07,536 --> 00:11:08,537
I'm just kidding.

324
00:11:08,624 --> 00:11:10,452
It says,
"911. Call now.

325
00:11:10,539 --> 00:11:12,846
"Urgent. About Martha.

326
00:11:12,933 --> 00:11:14,456
From Heaton Krupp."

327
00:11:14,543 --> 00:11:16,414
The developer
of the Granton Project.

328
00:11:18,416 --> 00:11:20,114
Oh, yeah.

329
00:11:20,201 --> 00:11:23,291
[Brewster]
'Do you enjoy police work?'

330
00:11:23,378 --> 00:11:24,858
Mm..

331
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,167
'Patrick?'

332
00:11:30,254 --> 00:11:31,386
Uh, yeah, I'm thinking.

333
00:11:31,473 --> 00:11:32,474
Uh..

334
00:11:33,954 --> 00:11:35,346
Yes and no.

335
00:11:35,433 --> 00:11:38,088
Uh, yeah, sometimes.

336
00:11:38,175 --> 00:11:40,047
Sometimes not.

337
00:11:40,134 --> 00:11:42,745
Forget it, Steve.

338
00:11:42,832 --> 00:11:44,225
Why do you so dislike
being filmed?

339
00:11:44,312 --> 00:11:45,530
Uh..

340
00:11:47,924 --> 00:11:50,666
'Cause you're
stealing my soul.

341
00:11:52,624 --> 00:11:54,844
So I called the mayor.
So what?

342
00:11:54,931 --> 00:11:57,455
I'm building a $20 million
complex in her town.

343
00:11:57,542 --> 00:11:58,805
I call her a lot.

344
00:11:58,892 --> 00:12:00,284
About Ms. St. Clare?

345
00:12:00,371 --> 00:12:03,287
About when I can start
construction again.

346
00:12:03,374 --> 00:12:05,072
This is costing me hundreds
of thousands of dollars.

347
00:12:05,159 --> 00:12:07,465
It cost
Ms. St. Clare a lot more.

348
00:12:07,552 --> 00:12:09,076
And I'm sorry about that.

349
00:12:09,163 --> 00:12:13,123
I am. But there's nothing
I can do about it.

350
00:12:13,210 --> 00:12:14,951
Martha would have
wanted us to go on.

351
00:12:15,038 --> 00:12:16,431
You knew her
well enough to know that?

352
00:12:16,518 --> 00:12:19,260
You're right.
I'm being pious.

353
00:12:19,347 --> 00:12:21,175
Maybe Martha would
have said, "Screw it."

354
00:12:21,262 --> 00:12:23,046
I knew her not at all
outside of business.

355
00:12:23,133 --> 00:12:25,832
Really? 'Cause we just got
her cellphone records

356
00:12:25,919 --> 00:12:27,703
and you called her
ten times yesterday.

357
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:29,618
Wanna tell us what you wanted to
talk about so urgently?

358
00:12:29,705 --> 00:12:31,533
Seems I should get my lawyer.
Have him sit in with us.

359
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:32,708
Sure. That's your right.

360
00:12:32,795 --> 00:12:33,927
Tell him
to bring all your

361
00:12:34,014 --> 00:12:35,189
permits for
the Granton Project.

362
00:12:35,276 --> 00:12:37,060
- My permits? Why?
- Why not?

363
00:12:37,147 --> 00:12:38,845
And we should make sure this
stays an active crime scene.

364
00:12:38,932 --> 00:12:40,020
Keep everyone out
until the case is solved.

365
00:12:40,107 --> 00:12:41,151
It could take weeks.

366
00:12:41,238 --> 00:12:42,936
See..

367
00:12:43,023 --> 00:12:44,807
We were talking
about money, okay?

368
00:12:44,894 --> 00:12:46,417
Ten million dollars
of public funds

369
00:12:46,504 --> 00:12:48,419
was to be released
when we broke ground.

370
00:12:48,506 --> 00:12:50,291
Then I heard rumors
that St. Clare

371
00:12:50,378 --> 00:12:52,728
was planning to tell the city
council to withhold them.

372
00:12:52,815 --> 00:12:55,600
- Why?
- I don't know!

373
00:12:55,687 --> 00:12:56,863
I mean, that's what
I was trying to find out.

374
00:12:56,950 --> 00:12:58,342
But St. Clare
was killed before

375
00:12:58,429 --> 00:12:59,343
she could talk
to the city council.

376
00:12:59,430 --> 00:13:00,867
Yes, but--

377
00:13:00,954 --> 00:13:02,216
So the $10 million will
come to you after all.

378
00:13:02,303 --> 00:13:04,305
What are you trying to
lay this on me?

379
00:13:04,392 --> 00:13:06,176
Because you're messing
with the wrong guy, officer!

380
00:13:06,263 --> 00:13:07,612
We're not officers.
We're agents.

381
00:13:07,699 --> 00:13:08,657
That's quite
a temper you got there.

382
00:13:08,744 --> 00:13:10,267
[glass shatters]

383
00:13:10,354 --> 00:13:11,660
Look out!

384
00:13:11,747 --> 00:13:14,532
Ah! My leg!

385
00:13:14,619 --> 00:13:15,969
- Grab him.
- Get down!

386
00:13:16,056 --> 00:13:17,405
Get on the floor!

387
00:13:17,492 --> 00:13:18,580
[shouting]

388
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,408
Put it out!
Put it out!

389
00:13:20,495 --> 00:13:21,713
Wayne, put it out.

390
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:23,150
Get the door!
Go, go, go, go!

391
00:13:23,237 --> 00:13:25,935
- Hang on!
- I got the door!

392
00:13:26,022 --> 00:13:26,936
[grunting]

393
00:13:28,198 --> 00:13:30,635
- Ah!
- You're fine.

394
00:13:30,722 --> 00:13:32,289
It's jammed!

395
00:13:32,376 --> 00:13:33,638
I got you.

396
00:13:33,725 --> 00:13:34,683
[glass shatters]

397
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:39,819
[coughs]

398
00:13:45,259 --> 00:13:46,042
[grunting]

399
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:52,048
[all coughing]

400
00:14:08,282 --> 00:14:09,239
This was done
by someone who knew

401
00:14:09,326 --> 00:14:10,284
what he or she was doing.

402
00:14:10,371 --> 00:14:12,895
[coughing]
Crackpot Jasper.

403
00:14:12,982 --> 00:14:15,202
He's a terrorist
and you ain't doing jack

404
00:14:15,289 --> 00:14:18,118
to catch him, chief.

405
00:14:18,205 --> 00:14:20,729
I'm in charge of the town
of Salter, Mr. Krupp.

406
00:14:20,816 --> 00:14:24,211
Not the outlying areas.

407
00:14:24,298 --> 00:14:25,560
Jasper's never
launched an attack here

408
00:14:25,647 --> 00:14:26,604
in town before.

409
00:14:26,691 --> 00:14:27,649
Until now.

410
00:14:27,736 --> 00:14:29,781
Hey! Check this out.

411
00:14:38,355 --> 00:14:39,966
Apparently, this is
the same tag that Jasper

412
00:14:40,053 --> 00:14:43,665
used in the attack
on the condos.

413
00:14:45,754 --> 00:14:46,929
This good, sir?

414
00:14:47,016 --> 00:14:47,974
[Brewster]
'It's great.'

415
00:14:48,061 --> 00:14:49,627
Uh, I've been
in fires before.

416
00:14:49,714 --> 00:14:52,239
I worked with the,
uh, Arson Squad in San Diego

417
00:14:52,326 --> 00:14:54,415
for a couple years, so..

418
00:14:54,502 --> 00:14:56,504
...I'm not unfamiliar
with the issues.

419
00:14:56,591 --> 00:14:58,636
It's never pleasant, though.

420
00:14:58,723 --> 00:15:01,378
Um...I mean, when you're,
when you're in it

421
00:15:01,465 --> 00:15:03,032
it's-there's no
time to think.

422
00:15:03,119 --> 00:15:07,036
But...but afterwards, well..

423
00:15:07,123 --> 00:15:09,299
...yeah.

424
00:15:09,386 --> 00:15:11,998
It can make you think.

425
00:15:12,085 --> 00:15:14,870
There was a..

426
00:15:14,957 --> 00:15:18,874
There was a moment
there, where, uh..

427
00:15:18,961 --> 00:15:20,093
[rattling]

428
00:15:21,833 --> 00:15:24,706
Yeah, makes you think.

429
00:15:26,229 --> 00:15:28,188
It's a gift, isn't it?

430
00:15:28,275 --> 00:15:30,973
Life.

431
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:34,281
You should be
grateful for it.

432
00:15:34,368 --> 00:15:36,283
Make the most of it.

433
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:38,502
We have to catch this guy
before he kills someone else.

434
00:15:38,589 --> 00:15:40,461
He hasn't killed anyone yet.

435
00:15:40,548 --> 00:15:42,158
- Not Martha St. Clare?
- Nah.

436
00:15:42,245 --> 00:15:44,204
Martha St. Clare was about
to stall the development.

437
00:15:44,291 --> 00:15:46,119
That exactly what Jasper
wants. So why kill her?

438
00:15:46,206 --> 00:15:48,512
[Lisbon]
'Maybe he didn't
know Martha's intentions.'

439
00:15:48,599 --> 00:15:52,429
But the mayor must have known.
Let's go see her.

440
00:15:52,516 --> 00:15:55,084
Yeah. You guys look
into this Jasper character.

441
00:15:55,171 --> 00:15:56,868
Don't bother.
He's a red herring.

442
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:58,435
What does that mean,
anyway, a red herring?

443
00:15:58,522 --> 00:16:00,220
A red herring
is what you look into

444
00:16:00,307 --> 00:16:02,700
regardless
of what Jane tells you.

445
00:16:02,787 --> 00:16:03,919
Anything on
the networks' footage?

446
00:16:04,006 --> 00:16:05,181
They've been
throwing up hurdles.

447
00:16:05,268 --> 00:16:07,053
Something about
first amendment issues.

448
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:09,272
Get the footage. I'm tired
of hearing their excuses.

449
00:16:09,359 --> 00:16:11,318
We ID somebody in the crowd,
maybe we get lucky.

450
00:16:11,405 --> 00:16:13,102
Yes, boss.

451
00:16:13,189 --> 00:16:15,017
Why am I a detective?
Why are you a reporter?

452
00:16:15,104 --> 00:16:16,366
[Brewster]
'What?'

453
00:16:16,453 --> 00:16:17,977
Why are you making
this documentary?

454
00:16:18,064 --> 00:16:19,630
'It's a fresh perspective
on law enforcement.'

455
00:16:19,717 --> 00:16:21,589
No, I mean,
what's in it for you?

456
00:16:21,676 --> 00:16:23,678
'Well, uh,
scoring this exclusive'

457
00:16:23,765 --> 00:16:25,201
'is a good way
to get noticed.'

458
00:16:25,288 --> 00:16:26,594
So you're ambitious.

459
00:16:26,681 --> 00:16:27,856
How long you been
doing the news here?

460
00:16:27,943 --> 00:16:29,379
- 'About eight years.'
- Anchor?

461
00:16:29,466 --> 00:16:30,902
'Mostly fieldwork.'

462
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:34,558
So you're ambitious,
but you haven't gotten very far.

463
00:16:34,645 --> 00:16:36,734
I, uh, I guess
that's about it, yeah.

464
00:16:36,821 --> 00:16:38,084
'Uh, you don't like'

465
00:16:38,171 --> 00:16:39,215
being asked
questions, do you?

466
00:16:39,302 --> 00:16:40,434
The team as a whole

467
00:16:40,521 --> 00:16:42,218
seems to have
a problem with that.

468
00:16:42,305 --> 00:16:43,480
Is that a question?

469
00:16:43,567 --> 00:16:46,005
Mike, if I can
interrupt here?

470
00:16:46,092 --> 00:16:47,571
- Yeah.
- We're clear.

471
00:16:47,658 --> 00:16:49,617
Uh, there's coffee
in the kitchen, John.

472
00:16:49,704 --> 00:16:51,358
I'm so sorry.

473
00:16:53,577 --> 00:16:55,188
- Agent Cho?
- Yeah?

474
00:16:55,275 --> 00:16:58,495
It is the specific
request of the deputy AG

475
00:16:58,582 --> 00:17:00,671
that your unit cooperate
fully with the media.

476
00:17:00,758 --> 00:17:01,846
What's your point?

477
00:17:01,933 --> 00:17:03,761
[coughs]

478
00:17:03,848 --> 00:17:05,024
[Rigsby clears throat]

479
00:17:05,633 --> 00:17:06,808
Oh.

480
00:17:16,296 --> 00:17:18,689
Mayor Shannon,
we need to talk.

481
00:17:18,776 --> 00:17:20,909
Of course. I have a meeting.
Please make it fast.

482
00:17:20,996 --> 00:17:21,953
Sure, how big
was your bribe

483
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,477
from Heaton Krupp?

484
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:28,308
That is an outrageous slander.

485
00:17:28,395 --> 00:17:30,832
You sold your approval
of the Granton Project.

486
00:17:30,919 --> 00:17:32,486
Martha found out,
she was gonna reveal it

487
00:17:32,573 --> 00:17:33,617
at the city
council meeting

488
00:17:33,704 --> 00:17:34,749
which you said
was gonna be

489
00:17:34,836 --> 00:17:37,273
about river rafting,
of all things.

490
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:40,189
River rafting,
from where did you pull that?

491
00:17:40,276 --> 00:17:43,018
You better have
really good personal lawyers.

492
00:17:43,105 --> 00:17:46,413
If you pursue this
absurd line of harassment

493
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:47,762
I will hang you
by your heels.

494
00:17:47,849 --> 00:17:49,024
Did you get
a slice, too?

495
00:17:49,111 --> 00:17:50,895
Or are you
strictly wage labor?

496
00:17:50,982 --> 00:17:52,506
Your superiors will hear
from our lawyers.

497
00:17:52,593 --> 00:17:53,898
Oh, don't bother
with lawyers.

498
00:17:53,985 --> 00:17:55,378
It's such a waste
of taxpayer dollars.

499
00:17:55,465 --> 00:17:57,380
Just confess.
You'll feel a lot better.

500
00:17:57,467 --> 00:18:00,688
In actuality, you have no proof
of this so-called bribery.

501
00:18:00,775 --> 00:18:01,819
Uh, none at all.

502
00:18:03,647 --> 00:18:06,389
Are all CBI agents
this incompetent?

503
00:18:06,476 --> 00:18:09,131
Have you even bothered to check
her lover as a suspect?

504
00:18:09,218 --> 00:18:11,394
First you say it was Jasper.
Now it's the lover that did it.

505
00:18:11,481 --> 00:18:12,917
- You gonna make up your mind?
- What lover?

506
00:18:13,004 --> 00:18:14,919
We understood
she had no social life.

507
00:18:15,006 --> 00:18:16,704
I didn't know she did.

508
00:18:16,791 --> 00:18:20,316
Oh, well, she did, and competent
police would have known that.

509
00:18:20,403 --> 00:18:22,623
Why didn't you tell us
this earlier?

510
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:26,061
Why don't I just do your job
foryou? How would that be?

511
00:18:26,148 --> 00:18:27,976
Oh, just please arrest her
or something.

512
00:18:28,063 --> 00:18:30,152
Nothing to hold her on.

513
00:18:30,239 --> 00:18:31,414
Eh.

514
00:18:32,372 --> 00:18:33,590
Eh.

515
00:18:35,505 --> 00:18:38,465
I'm the rookie on the team.

516
00:18:38,552 --> 00:18:42,425
Been here...18 months now.

517
00:18:42,512 --> 00:18:45,472
Um, it's hard work

518
00:18:45,559 --> 00:18:49,606
but this has been my dream
ever since I was a kid.

519
00:18:49,693 --> 00:18:51,782
To be a detective.

520
00:18:51,869 --> 00:18:53,915
'And what's been
the most surprising thing'

521
00:18:54,002 --> 00:18:56,352
'you've learned
about this job you do?'

522
00:18:59,181 --> 00:19:00,487
I've..

523
00:19:00,574 --> 00:19:04,404
...learned a lot about myself.

524
00:19:04,491 --> 00:19:08,712
As well as, about other people.

525
00:19:08,799 --> 00:19:12,586
Stuff...I wish
I didn't know sometimes.

526
00:19:12,673 --> 00:19:15,110
'Stuff like..'

527
00:19:15,197 --> 00:19:19,027
Why people do bad things
to one another.

528
00:19:19,114 --> 00:19:22,639
It's mainly because of secrets.

529
00:19:22,726 --> 00:19:25,773
Trying to hide the truth
chips away at your spirit.

530
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:29,342
Secrets ruin relationships.

531
00:19:29,429 --> 00:19:31,300
We finally got the footage from
every news station

532
00:19:31,387 --> 00:19:33,172
covering
the groundbreaking ceremony.

533
00:19:33,259 --> 00:19:35,086
Apparently, threats work.

534
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:37,306
These are two separate
vantage points of the mayor

535
00:19:37,393 --> 00:19:41,571
and these are feeds
of the crowd. There, that guy.

536
00:19:41,658 --> 00:19:44,357
[Lisbon]
'Can you narrow it down for us?
There's, like, 50 guys there.'

537
00:19:44,444 --> 00:19:46,837
The guy in the crowd there after
the mayor digs up the victim.

538
00:19:46,924 --> 00:19:49,405
He certainly doesn't
look like he fits in.

539
00:19:49,492 --> 00:19:51,451
"J."
That's bold.

540
00:19:51,538 --> 00:19:54,105
- A Jasper acolyte.
- Or the man himself.

541
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:56,586
Get with the local PD.
See if they can identify him.

542
00:19:59,807 --> 00:20:02,505
- 'What is it?'
- Nothing. Just hungry.

543
00:20:10,905 --> 00:20:12,559
So we went back
to St. Clare's apartment

544
00:20:12,646 --> 00:20:13,777
went through her closet
and realized

545
00:20:13,864 --> 00:20:15,388
that some of her work shirts--

546
00:20:15,475 --> 00:20:17,564
- Button on the right.
- Yeah, and not her size.

547
00:20:17,651 --> 00:20:19,043
So the mayor was right.
She did have a lover.

548
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:20,915
Of course she had a lover.

549
00:20:21,002 --> 00:20:23,004
That necklace she always wore
was obviously a romantic gift.

550
00:20:23,091 --> 00:20:24,875
She'd never spend
that kind of money on herself.

551
00:20:24,962 --> 00:20:27,138
Now you say so.
Very wise in hindsight.

552
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:28,662
Well, I thought
it went without saying.

553
00:20:28,749 --> 00:20:30,968
It's horribly obvious when
people are in a relationship

554
00:20:31,055 --> 00:20:34,885
impossible to hide,
try though they might.

555
00:20:34,972 --> 00:20:36,278
She was a very attractive woman.

556
00:20:36,365 --> 00:20:39,107
I would not be surprised
if she had two lovers.

557
00:20:39,194 --> 00:20:41,501
There is nothing here.
I'm gonna go out for lunch.

558
00:20:44,155 --> 00:20:46,897
Turn that thing off, or I will
shove it down your throat.

559
00:20:46,984 --> 00:20:49,987
Let's take a walk,
shall we? Come on.

560
00:21:01,695 --> 00:21:04,263
I know it hasn't been
the most pleasant experience

561
00:21:04,350 --> 00:21:06,265
having a camera crew here.

562
00:21:06,352 --> 00:21:08,571
But you gotta cooperate.
Deputy AG's orders.

563
00:21:08,658 --> 00:21:09,833
Yeah.

564
00:21:10,791 --> 00:21:12,662
So what's the deal?

565
00:21:12,749 --> 00:21:14,969
I would think out of everybody
you'd be the most comfortable

566
00:21:15,056 --> 00:21:16,318
with the cameras.

567
00:21:21,410 --> 00:21:22,933
Last time I was
in front of a camera

568
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:25,588
things, uh,
didn't turn out so well.

569
00:21:28,330 --> 00:21:29,897
Oh, God, Jane, I'm sorry.

570
00:21:29,984 --> 00:21:32,552
You don't need to be sorry.

571
00:21:32,639 --> 00:21:34,467
And you're right.

572
00:21:34,554 --> 00:21:36,904
There's no reason not to be
civil. I'm going to apologize.

573
00:21:42,779 --> 00:21:46,174
Hey, I'm sorry.
We didn't mean to be intrusive.

574
00:21:46,261 --> 00:21:48,698
No, I-I shouldn't
have snapped at you.

575
00:21:48,785 --> 00:21:53,050
I'm sorry. I just...I don't
like feeling spied on.

576
00:21:53,137 --> 00:21:55,183
It's my own little neurosis.

577
00:21:55,270 --> 00:21:56,489
You're just doing
your job, right?

578
00:21:56,576 --> 00:21:57,751
Right.

579
00:21:57,838 --> 00:21:59,666
Well, let me buy you a taco.

580
00:21:59,753 --> 00:22:01,276
- Sure.
- I know you're in.

581
00:22:01,363 --> 00:22:02,973
- I am kind of hungry.
- Well, that's the spirit.

582
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:04,932
I know the perfect place.
Vamonos.

583
00:22:09,284 --> 00:22:10,546
Muchas gracias.

584
00:22:13,462 --> 00:22:14,942
- Mike.
- Thank you.

585
00:22:15,029 --> 00:22:18,032
Steve. So tell me about
news gathering.

586
00:22:20,164 --> 00:22:21,862
Out of my way!

587
00:22:21,949 --> 00:22:23,733
Whoa! Whoa!

588
00:22:25,039 --> 00:22:26,170
[crowd screaming]

589
00:22:35,092 --> 00:22:37,486
Did you get that?
Did you get it?

590
00:22:42,839 --> 00:22:44,101
Keep moving.

591
00:22:49,106 --> 00:22:50,499
Let's go.

592
00:22:52,458 --> 00:22:55,025
I don't know where we're going,
but I hope there's a bathroom.

593
00:22:57,027 --> 00:22:58,420
I am busting.

594
00:22:59,682 --> 00:23:00,596
Oh.

595
00:23:02,511 --> 00:23:03,425
[chatter]

596
00:23:06,863 --> 00:23:07,821
Definitely Jasper.

597
00:23:07,908 --> 00:23:08,996
The description of the van

598
00:23:09,083 --> 00:23:10,519
matches one seen
near the condo fire

599
00:23:10,606 --> 00:23:12,391
and the luxury car lot
Jasper destroyed.

600
00:23:12,478 --> 00:23:14,610
How long has Chief Donner
had this information?

601
00:23:14,697 --> 00:23:15,872
Contact the local
and the county PD.

602
00:23:15,959 --> 00:23:17,265
On it.

603
00:23:17,352 --> 00:23:18,527
We got a hit on
the Jasper associate

604
00:23:18,614 --> 00:23:19,876
at the groundbreaking ceremony.

605
00:23:19,963 --> 00:23:21,400
Local activists
draw the line at kidnapping.

606
00:23:21,487 --> 00:23:23,184
- They gave this guy up fast.
- Bart Henrik.

607
00:23:23,271 --> 00:23:25,752
On his blog, he calls himself
a green warrior.

608
00:23:25,839 --> 00:23:27,928
He's been arrested several times
for inciting a riot

609
00:23:28,015 --> 00:23:29,886
public disorder and vandalism.

610
00:23:29,973 --> 00:23:31,627
- Go find him. Take Rigsby.
- You got it.

611
00:23:44,466 --> 00:23:45,815
Watch your step.

612
00:24:12,363 --> 00:24:13,626
I can see you mean business.

613
00:24:13,713 --> 00:24:15,192
Uh, there's no need
for firearms.

614
00:24:15,279 --> 00:24:16,759
I'm not Harry Houdini.

615
00:24:16,846 --> 00:24:17,760
Quiet.

616
00:24:20,371 --> 00:24:21,721
Thank you.

617
00:24:23,418 --> 00:24:24,767
So you're Jasper.

618
00:24:26,639 --> 00:24:28,075
Well, I'm honored.

619
00:24:31,339 --> 00:24:33,036
Please don't say
you kidnapped me for ransom

620
00:24:33,123 --> 00:24:36,300
because I-I doubt you'll get
$50, let alone save the whales.

621
00:24:36,387 --> 00:24:40,174
No ransom. In actuality,
just a simple message.

622
00:24:40,261 --> 00:24:42,306
I did not kill
Martha St. Clare

623
00:24:42,393 --> 00:24:45,353
and I didn't throw that
firebomb in Krupp's office.

624
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:48,051
Now, you, you are gonna
tell that to the police

625
00:24:48,138 --> 00:24:50,010
and to the media.

626
00:24:50,097 --> 00:24:52,578
So you kidnapped me
to proclaim your innocence.

627
00:24:52,665 --> 00:24:55,668
Have you ever heard
of a phone?

628
00:24:55,755 --> 00:24:57,844
Oh, yeah. I see.

629
00:24:57,931 --> 00:25:00,368
If you kidnap me
and I pass on the message

630
00:25:00,455 --> 00:25:03,110
then you get a blast of
that publicity that you love.

631
00:25:03,197 --> 00:25:04,503
If I am branded a killer

632
00:25:04,590 --> 00:25:07,680
everything I have fought
for is discredited.

633
00:25:07,767 --> 00:25:11,031
People support me because I have
respect for all living things.

634
00:25:11,118 --> 00:25:13,773
Yes, but it's
a good rule of thumb

635
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:17,298
to avoid doing things
that require you to wear a mask.

636
00:25:17,385 --> 00:25:19,779
And you're such a
handsome fellow, too.

637
00:25:22,956 --> 00:25:25,828
How'd you know
I'm handsome?

638
00:25:25,915 --> 00:25:27,569
Well, I was just speaking
figuratively.

639
00:25:27,656 --> 00:25:28,831
No, you weren't.

640
00:25:30,877 --> 00:25:32,792
- You know who I am.
- No, I have no idea.

641
00:25:34,271 --> 00:25:35,882
Leave us
and don't come back.

642
00:25:35,969 --> 00:25:37,448
'No, he doesn't have
to go anywhere.'

643
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:39,929
I-I-I.. Will you listen to me?
I have no idea.

644
00:25:40,016 --> 00:25:41,757
You could be Elvis Presley,
for all I know.

645
00:25:41,844 --> 00:25:43,237
- 'How did you know?'
- I don't know.

646
00:25:43,324 --> 00:25:44,543
How did you..

647
00:25:46,370 --> 00:25:48,285
Please don't do that.

648
00:25:57,860 --> 00:25:59,732
How did you know?

649
00:26:04,867 --> 00:26:07,740
Well, what's not to know?

650
00:26:07,827 --> 00:26:09,698
Your height,
your body language.

651
00:26:11,091 --> 00:26:12,483
Your syntax.

652
00:26:12,571 --> 00:26:14,094
You said "in actuality."

653
00:26:14,181 --> 00:26:16,357
I mean, who-who says
"in actuality?"

654
00:26:18,664 --> 00:26:19,795
Yes.

655
00:26:19,882 --> 00:26:20,796
Yeah.

656
00:26:21,884 --> 00:26:23,233
Very clever.

657
00:26:26,062 --> 00:26:27,934
So now we have a problem.

658
00:26:38,509 --> 00:26:40,555
Get that thing out of my face!

659
00:26:54,177 --> 00:26:55,439
Jasper kidnapped our colleague.

660
00:26:55,526 --> 00:26:57,441
- Where are they?
- Jasper who?

661
00:26:57,528 --> 00:26:58,529
Did you know you can
get more time

662
00:26:58,617 --> 00:27:00,531
for kidnapping
than murder?

663
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:01,707
That's crazy, right?

664
00:27:01,794 --> 00:27:02,838
And being an accessory
after the fact

665
00:27:02,925 --> 00:27:04,535
makes you just as guilty
as Jasper.

666
00:27:07,756 --> 00:27:10,716
Man, Jasper's avenging
Mother Earth. That's all.

667
00:27:10,803 --> 00:27:11,978
You know him well enough
to be sure of his motives.

668
00:27:12,065 --> 00:27:13,588
Yes.

669
00:27:13,675 --> 00:27:15,242
You know him so well you can
tell us where he might be.

670
00:27:15,329 --> 00:27:17,636
Even if I knew,
which I don't

671
00:27:17,723 --> 00:27:19,550
I would never betray Jasper.

672
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:21,465
- Never is a big word.
- Try me.

673
00:27:21,552 --> 00:27:24,033
What would Jane want us
to do in this situation, Cho?

674
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:25,556
With his life in jeopardy?

675
00:27:25,644 --> 00:27:26,645
You know what
he'd want us to do.

676
00:27:26,732 --> 00:27:28,516
Yep. Okay.

677
00:27:29,691 --> 00:27:31,954
I guess we have to go.
There.

678
00:27:37,612 --> 00:27:39,222
We should call an ambulance.
It's procedure.

679
00:27:39,309 --> 00:27:40,659
Sure. They can set it fast
and we can get

680
00:27:40,746 --> 00:27:41,703
straight back to questioning.

681
00:27:41,790 --> 00:27:43,618
Wait. Set what?

682
00:27:43,705 --> 00:27:45,141
[clanks]

683
00:27:45,228 --> 00:27:47,796
Your arm, you broke it,
slipped on the stairs.

684
00:27:47,883 --> 00:27:49,580
Yeah, you should
be more careful, Henrik.

685
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:53,149
Hey. Hey, a bunch of people
saw me come in here, fine.

686
00:27:53,236 --> 00:27:55,195
A bunch of cops,
and I'm one of them.

687
00:27:55,282 --> 00:27:57,023
I saw you fall.

688
00:27:57,110 --> 00:27:59,460
And every cop in this building
will say exactly the same.

689
00:28:00,504 --> 00:28:01,462
[thud]

690
00:28:13,169 --> 00:28:14,605
A cabin in the Sierra Foothills.

691
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:16,129
Ten miles northeast of Salter.

692
00:28:16,216 --> 00:28:17,565
Nice work.

693
00:28:20,176 --> 00:28:21,787
What to do?

694
00:28:21,874 --> 00:28:23,179
What to do?

695
00:28:23,266 --> 00:28:25,442
If I let you go now,
you'll rat me out.

696
00:28:25,529 --> 00:28:27,923
- If I may make a suggestion?
- No, you may not.

697
00:28:30,186 --> 00:28:32,319
Please, Wilson,
I can help.

698
00:28:32,406 --> 00:28:33,755
I cannot go to prison.

699
00:28:35,975 --> 00:28:38,020
I need to finish my work.
Don't you see?

700
00:28:38,107 --> 00:28:41,110
I do, I see, your work
is very important.

701
00:28:41,197 --> 00:28:43,678
But what I don't
understand though

702
00:28:43,765 --> 00:28:45,767
is why you were working
in the mayor's office.

703
00:28:45,854 --> 00:28:47,029
Where better
to study the enemy

704
00:28:47,116 --> 00:28:48,596
than from within
their very camp?

705
00:28:48,683 --> 00:28:50,076
Did you know that the mayor
was taking bribes

706
00:28:50,163 --> 00:28:51,817
from the developer Krupp?

707
00:28:51,904 --> 00:28:53,557
Of course.

708
00:28:53,644 --> 00:28:55,255
Who do you think
put Martha onto it?

709
00:28:55,342 --> 00:28:57,213
Ah. You told her.

710
00:28:59,128 --> 00:29:02,523
But why not expose the mayor
yourself or do it as Jasper?

711
00:29:02,610 --> 00:29:05,178
They would know that Jasper
was inside the mayor's office.

712
00:29:05,265 --> 00:29:07,615
They would soon suspect me.

713
00:29:07,702 --> 00:29:10,705
I work in the shadows,
that's why I am still here.

714
00:29:10,792 --> 00:29:11,880
Still fighting.

715
00:29:11,967 --> 00:29:13,360
I understand.

716
00:29:14,404 --> 00:29:15,797
Let me help you.

717
00:29:15,884 --> 00:29:17,973
Don't try to play me.

718
00:29:18,060 --> 00:29:20,410
Don't go saying you won't tell
on me if I set you free

719
00:29:20,497 --> 00:29:21,672
because I know you will.

720
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:24,327
Wilson, I am not trying
to play you.

721
00:29:24,414 --> 00:29:27,069
I will not play you.

722
00:29:27,156 --> 00:29:29,855
I understand and respect
your intelligence.

723
00:29:31,508 --> 00:29:32,858
Have a seat.

724
00:29:33,946 --> 00:29:35,208
Just take a moment.

725
00:29:52,573 --> 00:29:53,922
Wilson, look at me.

726
00:29:54,705 --> 00:29:56,055
I can help you.

727
00:29:59,536 --> 00:30:01,321
How?

728
00:30:01,408 --> 00:30:03,802
Look at me.

729
00:30:03,889 --> 00:30:05,804
You can see that
I'm telling the truth.

730
00:30:09,198 --> 00:30:11,200
I want what you want.

731
00:30:12,419 --> 00:30:13,986
Peace and harmony.

732
00:30:15,683 --> 00:30:16,989
'Peace..'

733
00:30:18,425 --> 00:30:19,382
...quiet.

734
00:30:22,385 --> 00:30:24,344
It's easy.

735
00:30:24,431 --> 00:30:25,824
You can have it.

736
00:30:28,914 --> 00:30:30,872
'If you want it,
you can have it.'

737
00:30:33,919 --> 00:30:35,355
So peaceful.

738
00:30:38,314 --> 00:30:41,622
'This is Chief Donner of
the Salter Police Department!'

739
00:30:41,709 --> 00:30:43,667
'You're completely surrounded.
Come out with your hands up!'

740
00:30:43,754 --> 00:30:45,104
Stay cool.

741
00:30:56,724 --> 00:30:58,378
Just stay cool.

742
00:31:07,604 --> 00:31:08,562
Go.

743
00:31:10,433 --> 00:31:12,435
- Clear!
- Clear!

744
00:31:12,522 --> 00:31:15,134
There's a trap door.

745
00:31:15,221 --> 00:31:16,918
- I got him.
- Lisbon?

746
00:31:17,005 --> 00:31:19,051
- Jane.
- Wow, I'm impressed.

747
00:31:19,138 --> 00:31:20,617
How the hell did you
find me out here?

748
00:31:20,704 --> 00:31:22,489
Right, because
we're lost without you?

749
00:31:22,576 --> 00:31:24,491
I wouldn't say that,
but I'm still impressed.

750
00:31:24,578 --> 00:31:26,014
- Wait. D-Don't move.
- Oh.

751
00:31:26,101 --> 00:31:28,060
They could have
booby-trapped the place.

752
00:31:28,147 --> 00:31:29,800
We'll have the bomb squad
take a look at you.

753
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:32,325
What? Oh, you're kidding.
You're kidding.

754
00:31:32,412 --> 00:31:33,761
I'm-I'm thankful and all that

755
00:31:33,848 --> 00:31:35,154
'but just get me out of here'

756
00:31:35,241 --> 00:31:36,285
'and I'll tell you the story.'

757
00:31:36,372 --> 00:31:37,808
- What story?
- Ahh.

758
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:47,514
- So we know who Jasper is.
- Fonteneau.

759
00:31:47,601 --> 00:31:49,081
No trace of him. Slipped right
through the locals' hands.

760
00:31:49,168 --> 00:31:50,560
He's one guy,
for crying out loud.

761
00:31:50,647 --> 00:31:52,432
He obviously knows
those woods a lot better.

762
00:31:52,519 --> 00:31:53,824
Jane, enough recovery time.

763
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:55,304
Tell us about Fonteneau.
What'd he say?

764
00:31:55,391 --> 00:31:58,394
Well, he sprouted
a lot of nonsense, denial.

765
00:31:58,481 --> 00:32:00,396
Truth is, he took the job
in the mayor's office

766
00:32:00,483 --> 00:32:03,269
to plan targeted attacks
on new developments around town.

767
00:32:03,356 --> 00:32:05,793
He and St. Clare became lovers.

768
00:32:05,880 --> 00:32:06,837
Secret boyfriend.

769
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:08,230
But when St. Clare found out

770
00:32:08,317 --> 00:32:10,537
about Fonteneau's
secret life as Jasper

771
00:32:10,624 --> 00:32:12,800
he killed her for it,
to keep her quiet.

772
00:32:12,887 --> 00:32:14,802
I'll check on the warrant
for Fonteneau's place.

773
00:32:14,889 --> 00:32:17,413
Get everybody briefed,
suited up and ready to roll.

774
00:32:17,500 --> 00:32:18,762
Oh, look for
St. Clare's necklace.

775
00:32:18,849 --> 00:32:20,677
It was a gift from Fonteneau.

776
00:32:20,764 --> 00:32:23,419
[Patrick]
'My guess, he took it
when he killed her. We need it.'

777
00:32:23,506 --> 00:32:26,248
You guys sit on the location
until the warrant comes in.

778
00:32:29,860 --> 00:32:31,384
Chief Donner?
Yeah, i-it's Lisbon.

779
00:32:31,471 --> 00:32:33,821
Oh, I need some Aspirin.

780
00:32:33,908 --> 00:32:35,692
[Lisbon]
'Yeah.'

781
00:32:35,779 --> 00:32:39,131
Yeah, I-I just wanted..
could you hold on, chief?

782
00:32:39,218 --> 00:32:41,568
Look, that's enough, guys.
We're done filming.

783
00:32:41,655 --> 00:32:43,613
You know, catching
the bad guy would be

784
00:32:43,700 --> 00:32:46,747
a great end of the show, make
you guys look like superstars.

785
00:32:46,834 --> 00:32:49,402
Well, it'd certainly make
the deputy AG very happy.

786
00:32:49,489 --> 00:32:50,446
True.

787
00:32:51,839 --> 00:32:53,275
Alright,
you can film the bust

788
00:32:53,362 --> 00:32:55,625
but you have to do
exactly what I say.

789
00:32:55,712 --> 00:32:57,062
Deal.

790
00:32:57,149 --> 00:32:58,280
Meet me at Fonteneau's
at 06:00 hours.

791
00:32:58,367 --> 00:33:00,543
- Yes, ma'am.
- Hey, chief.

792
00:33:00,630 --> 00:33:02,241
We're gonna need assistance
from your entry team again.

793
00:33:27,570 --> 00:33:28,528
[sighs]

794
00:33:53,161 --> 00:33:54,641
What now?

795
00:33:54,728 --> 00:33:56,469
We set a perimeter
and wait for the warrant.

796
00:33:56,556 --> 00:33:58,906
Yeah, there's a lot
of this kind of stuff.

797
00:33:58,993 --> 00:34:01,256
Not too many car chases.

798
00:34:03,519 --> 00:34:06,087
Maybe we could, uh, ask a few
questions while we're waiting?

799
00:34:07,784 --> 00:34:08,916
Uh..

800
00:34:11,179 --> 00:34:13,573
Sure. If you must.

801
00:34:16,228 --> 00:34:17,620
[clears throat]

802
00:34:17,707 --> 00:34:21,624
Um, how did you come
to work with the CBI?

803
00:34:21,711 --> 00:34:23,061
You know how.

804
00:34:23,148 --> 00:34:24,366
Yes, but I-I need you
to say it to the camera.

805
00:34:24,453 --> 00:34:26,064
Yeah, yeah,
I-I see. I got it.

806
00:34:28,501 --> 00:34:30,155
[sighs]

807
00:34:30,242 --> 00:34:32,244
Um..

808
00:34:32,331 --> 00:34:33,854
Well, I came
to work with the CBI

809
00:34:33,941 --> 00:34:37,336
after my wife and child
were murdered.

810
00:34:48,825 --> 00:34:50,827
Have you ever
experienced loss like that?

811
00:34:51,959 --> 00:34:54,004
A loss of love?

812
00:34:57,182 --> 00:35:00,185
There's nothing more important
than love, is there?

813
00:35:00,272 --> 00:35:01,664
Well, we're talking about you.

814
00:35:01,751 --> 00:35:02,839
Yeah.

815
00:35:06,539 --> 00:35:08,193
It can be very hard
when love goes away.

816
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:10,891
It's like a...a betrayal.

817
00:35:12,893 --> 00:35:15,069
Almost like a
violent act, right?

818
00:35:16,462 --> 00:35:19,856
- Right?
- I guess.

819
00:35:19,943 --> 00:35:22,859
Um, why don't-why don't
we go back to, um--

820
00:35:22,946 --> 00:35:25,688
When you give someone your heart
and they throw it aside

821
00:35:25,775 --> 00:35:28,517
it's natural to be angry.

822
00:35:28,604 --> 00:35:31,868
Especially when you've come
to rely on 'em.

823
00:35:31,955 --> 00:35:35,829
When your career
is tied to theirs.

824
00:35:35,916 --> 00:35:37,526
I don't know
what you're..

825
00:35:37,613 --> 00:35:39,137
Why don't you show us
what you got in your pockets?

826
00:35:39,224 --> 00:35:41,704
- What?
- You heard me.

827
00:35:41,791 --> 00:35:43,532
- No.
- Why not?

828
00:35:45,404 --> 00:35:46,796
Because you don't
have the right.

829
00:35:46,883 --> 00:35:48,972
Okay.

830
00:35:49,059 --> 00:35:52,715
Okay. I'll tell you
what you have in your pocket

831
00:35:52,802 --> 00:35:54,413
and you tell me if I'm right.

832
00:35:54,500 --> 00:35:56,502
In your pocket, you have
a blue topaz necklace

833
00:35:56,589 --> 00:35:57,894
that you once gave
to Martha St. Clare

834
00:35:57,981 --> 00:35:59,418
when you were lovers.

835
00:35:59,505 --> 00:36:02,334
You took that necklace back
after you killed her.

836
00:36:02,421 --> 00:36:06,076
You were gonna plant it
in Fonteneau's house.

837
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:08,949
Prompted by
my cunningly brilliant ruse.

838
00:36:14,259 --> 00:36:15,347
Aha.

839
00:36:16,609 --> 00:36:19,786
Aha. That's it.

840
00:36:19,873 --> 00:36:21,440
I don't know
how that got in there.

841
00:36:21,527 --> 00:36:24,356
Oh, please. Don't be so silly.
Arrest him, Cho.

842
00:36:24,443 --> 00:36:27,359
Get on your knees.
Put your hands on your head.

843
00:36:27,446 --> 00:36:28,882
Now!

844
00:36:32,102 --> 00:36:33,887
Get up.

845
00:36:33,974 --> 00:36:35,323
That's for you.

846
00:36:36,455 --> 00:36:37,847
And this..

847
00:36:40,023 --> 00:36:41,460
...is for me.

848
00:36:46,726 --> 00:36:48,467
Here it comes.

849
00:36:49,772 --> 00:36:52,514
Bang. There.
You looked away.

850
00:36:52,601 --> 00:36:54,603
Martha St. Clare's body
hasn't been revealed

851
00:36:54,690 --> 00:36:57,389
and you looked away, because you
knew what was gonna happen

852
00:36:57,476 --> 00:37:00,000
because you buried that body
at that building site

853
00:37:00,087 --> 00:37:03,743
and you firebombed the trailer
to try and frame Jasper.

854
00:37:03,830 --> 00:37:07,268
You're too clever, Mike,
you're just too clever.

855
00:37:07,355 --> 00:37:10,053
Nah. You spout
a lot of theory

856
00:37:10,140 --> 00:37:12,273
but no legal proof.

857
00:37:12,360 --> 00:37:15,624
You want legal proof?
The lab reports came back.

858
00:37:15,711 --> 00:37:18,801
They found traces of Martha's
blood in the trunk of your car.

859
00:37:21,500 --> 00:37:23,850
[Lisbon]
'Do you want to tell us
what happened?'

860
00:37:33,163 --> 00:37:35,514
Rumors said
the mayor was dirty

861
00:37:35,601 --> 00:37:37,994
but there was no proof.

862
00:37:38,081 --> 00:37:39,518
I knew something was up.

863
00:37:39,605 --> 00:37:43,957
But...no matter
how much I pushed her

864
00:37:44,044 --> 00:37:47,308
Martha wouldn't
say anything. Nothing.

865
00:37:49,223 --> 00:37:52,313
And last night..

866
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:55,055
I was going through
her computers.

867
00:37:55,142 --> 00:37:58,624
Checking on some stuff,
you know?

868
00:37:58,711 --> 00:38:02,584
I found this speech
she was preparing to give

869
00:38:02,671 --> 00:38:05,370
exposing the mayor,
as corrupt.

870
00:38:05,457 --> 00:38:06,762
With proof.

871
00:38:06,849 --> 00:38:09,678
Facts and figures,
the whole deal.

872
00:38:09,765 --> 00:38:11,898
And she kept it from me
the whole time.

873
00:38:11,985 --> 00:38:16,119
This is a story
that could've made my career.

874
00:38:16,206 --> 00:38:17,991
'I have been waiting
for a story like this'

875
00:38:18,078 --> 00:38:20,210
'my whole life.'

876
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:23,692
And she's mad 'cause
I'm on her computer.Hello.

877
00:38:23,779 --> 00:38:25,520
So she..

878
00:38:27,783 --> 00:38:30,743
She said, uh, she couldn't trust
me anymore and that it was over.

879
00:38:31,787 --> 00:38:33,789
The argument escalated

880
00:38:33,876 --> 00:38:37,315
and, uh, I took
my necklace back.

881
00:38:37,402 --> 00:38:39,621
And then she starts
taunting me.

882
00:38:41,406 --> 00:38:43,712
Implying that
I don't have what it takes

883
00:38:43,799 --> 00:38:47,020
to be in the big leagues
anyway.

884
00:38:47,107 --> 00:38:49,022
Saying I'm a loser.

885
00:38:49,109 --> 00:38:51,329
She's had enough?

886
00:38:51,416 --> 00:38:54,375
She's had enough? She has?

887
00:38:54,462 --> 00:38:56,029
No, no, no, no.

888
00:38:56,116 --> 00:38:58,031
I've had enough. Me!

889
00:39:06,735 --> 00:39:08,346
Well..

890
00:39:08,433 --> 00:39:10,522
We'll take that
as a confession.

891
00:39:10,609 --> 00:39:13,655
In a stunning revelation,
Mayor Melba Walker Shannon

892
00:39:13,742 --> 00:39:16,832
'has been arrested by the DA
for corruption charges'

893
00:39:16,919 --> 00:39:19,531
stemming from the Granton
at Salter development.

894
00:39:19,618 --> 00:39:22,447
The accuser is her
closest aide, Wilson Fonteneau

895
00:39:22,534 --> 00:39:24,100
'who agreed to testify
against the mayor'

896
00:39:24,187 --> 00:39:26,276
in exchange for leniency

897
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:29,454
regarding his activities
as eco-terrorist Jasper.

898
00:39:29,541 --> 00:39:31,499
'This only
the latest development'

899
00:39:31,586 --> 00:39:33,849
in a bizarre story
of murder and greed

900
00:39:33,936 --> 00:39:36,591
that has captivated
the Central Valley.

901
00:39:36,678 --> 00:39:38,158
Hey. I was enjoying that.

902
00:39:38,245 --> 00:39:40,508
Ugh. I hate how they
over-dramatize everything.

903
00:39:40,595 --> 00:39:41,727
Yeah, I hate that.

904
00:39:41,814 --> 00:39:43,337
Captivated the Central Valley.

905
00:39:43,424 --> 00:39:46,949
- Give me a break.
- Doughnuts.

906
00:39:47,036 --> 00:39:48,690
Ladies first.

907
00:39:48,777 --> 00:39:51,040
So, uh, guys?

908
00:39:51,127 --> 00:39:54,174
Uh, I have something to say.

909
00:39:54,261 --> 00:39:57,003
Wehave something to say.

910
00:39:57,090 --> 00:40:01,007
Uh, life's too short
for dishonesty.

911
00:40:01,094 --> 00:40:04,706
Van Pelt..
Grace and I are lovers.

912
00:40:08,449 --> 00:40:10,843
No, you're not.

913
00:40:10,930 --> 00:40:14,760
- Um, yes, we are.
- No, you are not lovers.

914
00:40:14,847 --> 00:40:16,152
Uh, but we are, though.

915
00:40:16,239 --> 00:40:18,067
No, you're not.

916
00:40:18,154 --> 00:40:19,504
Because a sexual relationship

917
00:40:19,591 --> 00:40:21,984
between two fellow
bureau employees

918
00:40:22,071 --> 00:40:24,030
is strictly against the rules.

919
00:40:24,117 --> 00:40:26,162
Which is why
we kept it a secret.

920
00:40:26,249 --> 00:40:30,253
But we don't want
to live a lie anymore.

921
00:40:30,340 --> 00:40:31,603
Come what may.

922
00:40:31,690 --> 00:40:33,300
[chuckles]

923
00:40:35,520 --> 00:40:37,522
Well, it's a big secret.
Well kept.

924
00:40:37,609 --> 00:40:39,045
Maybe you knew,
but nobody else did.

925
00:40:39,132 --> 00:40:40,307
I knew.
Half the building knows.

926
00:40:40,394 --> 00:40:41,395
- They do not.
- 'Yes they do.'

927
00:40:41,482 --> 00:40:42,483
The only person that didn't know

928
00:40:42,570 --> 00:40:44,050
is glaring at you right now.

929
00:40:44,137 --> 00:40:46,487
And now I have
to do something about it.

930
00:40:46,574 --> 00:40:50,186
- What are you gonna do?
- Yeah, whatareyou gonna do?

931
00:40:55,322 --> 00:40:56,671
I'm thinking.

932
00:40:58,630 --> 00:40:59,544
'Go.'

933
00:41:13,688 --> 00:41:16,299
[male narrator]
Stay tuned for scenes
from our next episode.

934
00:41:19,085 --> 00:41:19,999
[theme music]

